This thesis investigates the impact of contamination on anomaly detection systems. We analyzed aggregated metrics to determine performance baselines.

The correlation matrix reveals significant dependencies between feature sets.

Local Outlier Factor (LOF) sensitivity was evaluated via k-sweep analysis.

Finally, we compared our approach against State-of-the-Art (SOTA) models using the provided comparison table.

For implementation details, see the configuration in code/config.py.

### References to Data and Code

- Aggregated Metrics: \ref_csv{results/aggregated_metrics.csv}
- Correlation Matrix: \ref_csv{results/correlation_matrix.csv}
- LOF K-Sweep: \ref_csv{results/lof_k_sweep.csv}
- SOTA Comparison: \ref_csv{results/sota_comparison_table.csv}
- Configuration Code: \ref_ast{code/config.py}

